From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:47:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-24: drag and drop in the component tree moves a
 component into another container (0.24.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF document outline: drag components (the multi-selection too) in the 元件
tree and drop them
- onto a TPanel / TGroupBox / TTabSheet / the form (or the empty area): they
  move into it, at its end (on top) -- into a generated group box's
  <div class="cli">;
- onto any other component: they move next to it, into its parent.
Their left/top numbers stay (they now count from the new container). Never
into itself or into something inside it; a locked one does not move. One
WorkspaceEdit (one Ctrl+Z), the page re-drawn, the moved one selected.
- ComponentDnd: a TreeDragAndDropController on the tree's own mime type; the
  names travel in the DataTransfer, the drop runs cmdReparent.

Tests: smoke 87 (spbSave onto GroupBox1: into it, out of Panel2, once,
selected; Panel2 onto its own spbSave refused; onto XST1: right after it),
real VS Code 86 (the real DataTransfer: spbSave into GroupBox1, the re-drawn
tree has it there; one undo puts it back; NO-SAVES), lib 116, probe, panels
-- all pass. (tools/wb_serve.cpp changed during the run by another session:
the launcher's WARN, as it should.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
